---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import { RATES_SNAPSHOT } from '../../lib/site';
import { defaultParams, featuredProb } from '../../lib/pity';

const p90 = defaultParams('character');
const demo90Off = featuredProb({ ...p90, radiance: false }, 90);
const demo90On = featuredProb({ ...p90, state: 'armed' }, 90);

const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'Article',
    headline: 'Capturing Radiance Explained: The 55% 50/50 in Genshin Impact',
    description:
      'Since Genshin Impact 5.0, Capturing Radiance converts some losing 50/50s into wins, raising the consolidated featured-character probability from 50% to about 55%. How it works and how to plan with it.',
    datePublished: '2026-10-11',
    author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'PityHub' },
    publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'PityHub' },
    mainEntityOfPage: 'https://pitycalc.top/guides/capturing-radiance/',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Capturing Radiance Explained - Genshin's ~55% 50/50 (v5.0+)"
  description={`Capturing Radiance (Genshin Impact 5.0+) rescues some losing 50/50s, lifting the featured-character probability from 50% to ~55% consolidated. How it works, the community data, and how to plan around it. Snapshot ${RATES_SNAPSHOT}.`}
  path="/guides/capturing-radiance/"
  ogType="article"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <div class="container">
    <Breadcrumbs crumbs={[{ href: '/guides/', label: 'Guides' }, { label: 'Capturing Radiance' }]} />
    <article class="prose">
      <span class="overline">Guide</span>
      <h1>Capturing Radiance, explained</h1>
      <p>
        For four years the character banner's central drama was a literal coin flip: every 5★ was
        the featured character 50% of the time, and a loss only promised the next one. Version 5.0
        quietly tilted the coin. <b>Capturing Radiance</b> (命定常驻 in the CN client) can convert
        a losing 50/50 into a win on the spot - you'll see a distinctive golden animation instead
        of the usual heartbreak - raising the official consolidated probability of the featured
        character from 50% to about <b>55%</b>.
      </p>

      <h2><Icon name="info" size={19} /> How it actually works</h2>
      <p>
        HoYoverse's official description is short: when you would lose a 50/50, Radiance may
        trigger and guarantee the featured character instead, with the effect that the
        consolidated featured probability rises to ≈55%. The community has filled in the blanks
        from large wish-export datasets: the rescue fires on roughly <b>10% of losing 50/50s</b>
        (0.5 + 0.5 × 0.10 = 0.55), and - per several analyses - it seems to arm after you've
        recently lost a 50/50, preferentially rescuing players on loss streaks (some threads argue
        it only fires on the 3rd–4th consecutive loss). The official FAQ insists there are no
        hidden conditions beyond the base rates.
      </p>
      <p>
        For planning purposes the distinction barely matters, and our calculator exposes both
        knobs: a <b>50/50 state</b> (won last / lost last / guaranteed) and a
        <b>Radiance toggle</b>. The “lost last” state models the armed 50/50 you enter after
        taking a guaranteed pull - that's the one Radiance can rescue at 55%.
      </p>

      <h2><Icon name="trending-up" size={19} /> What it changes - in wishes</h2>
      <p>
        Radiance is comfort, not revolution. On the armed 50/50 after a loss, your odds within a
        90-wish budget move from {(demo90Off * 100).toFixed(1)}% to {(demo90On * 100).toFixed(1)}%
        in our model. The worst case is untouched: <b>180 wishes still guarantees</b> a character
        from a fresh 50/50, because Radiance can't fire on a guarantee. Expected cost drifts down
        by a couple of wishes per character - nice, not life-changing.
      </p>

      <h2><Icon name="bulb" size={19} /> Planning with Radiance</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Realistic mode:</b> leave Radiance on (default) - it matches the official 55% consolidated figure.</li>
        <li><b>Conservative mode:</b> switch it off when deciding the minimum bank needed; the guarantee math is identical either way.</li>
        <li><b>Never count on the animation:</b> budget as if every 50/50 is 50/50; treat any rescue as a bonus wish refund.</li>
      </ul>

      <p class="note-src">
        Model, parameters and sources on the <a href="/methodology/">methodology page</a>.
        Snapshot {RATES_SNAPSHOT}. Try your exact situation in the
        <a href="/pity-calculator/">pity calculator</a>, or feel the mechanic in the
        <a href="/simulator/">50/50 simulator</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
